    {
      "source_id": "x:thorstenball",
      "type": "x",
      "handle": "thorstenball",
      "name": "Thorsten Ball",
      "items": [
        {
          "published_at": "2026-10-23T03:59:38.487Z",
          "url": "https://x.com/thorstenball/status/2113480441537995037",
          "topic": "Internal agent platforms",
          "text": "Raise your hand if you work in a 2010s SaaS company that has built their own agent platform that no one really wants to use.",
          "quote_tweet": {
            "url": "https://x.com/ajkemps/status/2113470734588641681",
            "published_at": "2026-10-23T03:21:04.170Z",
            "author": {
              "name": "Alex Kemper",
              "handle": "ajkemps"
            },
            "text": "To be direct about it: every company that considers themselves a “tech” company is currently building a much worse version of something they could buy off the shelf, and furthermore they often have several teams competing on this front\n\nThen they launch it after 3-6 months of building in a silo and can’t get their colleagues to use it for entirely predictable reasons\n\nCoding agents and their adjacent products are among the most competitive markets of all time. The benefits of a highly competitive market accrue to customers by virtue of this intense competition among suppliers. Econ 101\n\nIs the internal team working on your agent platform really keeping pace with the market? Even if they put in the same hours (they don’t), they don’t have the breadth of customers and hard contact with the market to get the feedback necessary to make the product any good\n\nBig corporates that call their devs “IT” don’t delude themselves in this way. They buy the best, recognize their relative advantage (vendors will build almost anything for you because the competitive pressures demand it), and get back to work",
            "media": []
          },
          "author_replies": [],
          "render_audit": {
            "root_article_url": "https://x.com/thorstenball/status/2113480441537995037",
            "inspected_at": "2026-10-23T04:05:00Z",
